namespace Spek.Cluster;

/// <summary>
/// State of a peer node in the cluster, as observed by the local node.
/// Borrowed wholesale from Akka.Cluster (which itself adapted SWIM):
/// nodes transition through these states as gossip / handshakes /
/// failure-detector signals arrive.
///
/// <para>Transitions are driven by <c>StaticSeedClusterMembership</c>,
/// which uses upfront-configured peers and shutdown-time leave gossip;
/// no full SWIM gossip implementation exists. That is
/// enough for the state machine + cluster-view API to be exercised
/// end-to-end without a full SWIM impl).</para>
/// </summary>
enum NodeState
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Initial state for a node we've heard about (via seed-config)
    /// but haven't successfully connected to yet. `Cluster.MarkPeerUp`
    /// advances the state to <see cref="Up"/> once the transport
    /// handshake completes.
    /// </summary>
    Joining,

    /// <summary>
    /// Steady-state. The peer has completed its handshake and accepts
    /// inbound traffic. The vast majority of the time a healthy cluster
    /// member sits here.
    /// </summary>
    Up,

    /// <summary>
    /// The peer announced its intent to leave gracefully. Once
    /// in-flight traffic drains, the state advances to
    /// <see cref="Exiting"/>.
    /// </summary>
    Leaving,

    /// <summary>
    /// The peer is in the process of shutting down. No new sends
    /// accepted; any in-flight responses still flow back. After all
    /// outstanding work drains the state advances to <see cref="Down"/>.
    /// </summary>
    Exiting,

    /// <summary>
    /// The peer stopped responding without a graceful leave. It may
    /// come back (see <c>ClusterEvent.NodeReachableAgain</c>). Sends to
    /// an unreachable node surface through the transport's
    /// <c>DeliveryFailed</c> event.
    /// </summary>
    Unreachable,

    /// <summary>
    /// The peer is permanently offline: it gracefully exited, or the
    /// caller marked it down after deciding it will not return.
    /// </summary>
    Down,
}
